Suggests: chromium
Description: MapleStory TW (Taiwan) launcher for Linux
 maple-cask runs the Taiwanese MapleStory client with a patched wine runner
 inside gamescope, and logs in with beanfun OTP (QR code or passkey).
 The wine runner, DXVK and the game itself (about 70GB) are downloaded per
 user by "maple update" / "maple install" into ~/.local/share/maplestory-tw.
 .
 This package changes a kernel setting: it installs
 /usr/lib/sysctl.d/99-maple-cask.conf with kernel.split_lock_mitigate = 0
 (also applied immediately on install), because the game's anti-cheat
 triggers split locks and the kernel's default penalty causes periodic
 stutter. It also loads the ntsync module at boot (/usr/lib/modules-load.d).
